{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":667,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Ezra.5","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Ezra","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Ezra 5","reference":"Ezra 5","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"Zerubbabel encouraged by Haggai and Zechariah, sets the work forward again, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":2,"text":"1, 2.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":3,"text":"Their adversaries oppose them again, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":4,"text":"3-5.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":5,"text":"Write to Darius, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":6,"text":"6-17.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":7,"text":"1.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":8,"text":"The son - His grand-child; for he was the son of Baraciah.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":9,"text":"Prophesied - Commanding them from God to return to building the temple, with a promise of his favour and assistance.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":10,"text":"2.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":11,"text":"Helping - Encouraging the people to work by their presence, and assurance of success.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":12,"text":"It is supposed, the work had stopt about fifteen years.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":13,"text":"The first chapter of Haggai is the best comment on these two verses.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":14,"text":"3.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":15,"text":"Shethar-boznai - Not Rehum and Shimshai, &c. who were either dead, or removed from their office by Darius.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":16,"text":"4.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":17,"text":"We - Jews.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":18,"text":"Accordingly - According to what they asked.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":19,"text":"That made this building - That were the undertakers and encouragers of it.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":20,"text":"8.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":21,"text":"Great God - And indeed, thus far the greater part of the Samaritans agreed with them.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":22,"text":"17.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":23,"text":"Now therefore. &c. - If the case had been so fairly stated to Artaxerxes, he would hardly have hindered the work.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":24,"text":"The people of God could not be persecuted, if they were not belied.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Ezra","chapter":5}}